    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Create a personalized newsletter welcome email for this new subscriber.\n\nSubscriber information:\n\nFull Name: {{ $json['Full name'] }}\nMobile Number: {{ $('On form submission').item.json['Mobile Number'] }}\nEmail: {{ $('On form submission').item.json['Email Address'] }}\nSubmission Date: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.submittedAt }}\n\nWrite a friendly, professional welcome message that:\n- Welcomes the subscriber to the newsletter\n- Thanks them for subscribing\n- Briefly explains what they can expect from the newsletter\n- Uses their first name or full name naturally\n- Does not invent specific products, offers, discounts, or company information\n- Keeps the message concise and professional\n\nReturn only the email content. Do not include a subject line.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a professional email newsletter designer and copywriter.\n\nYour task is to create a polished, attractive HTML newsletter email for a new subscriber.\n\nFollow these requirements exactly:\n\n- Return ONLY the complete HTML email.\n- Do NOT use Markdown.\n- Do NOT include ```html or any code fences.\n- The HTML must be compatible with Gmail.\n- Use inline CSS only.\n- Do not use JavaScript.\n- Do not use external CSS, fonts, or images.\n- Use tables where appropriate for reliable email rendering.\n- Use a maximum content width of 600px.\n- Make the email readable on both desktop and mobile devices.\n- Keep the design modern, clean, professional, and technology-focused.\n- Include a clear headline.\n- Include a short personalized welcome message.\n- Thank the subscriber for joining the newsletter.\n- Briefly explain what they can expect from the newsletter.\n- Include a natural call-to-action.\n- Include a simple professional footer.\n- Use the subscriber's name naturally.\n- Do not invent personal information, products, services, offers, discounts, statistics, or company claims that were not provided.\n- Do not include the subscriber's private information unnecessarily in the visible email.\n- Do not include a subject line.\n\nBrand:\nSakhawat NES Newsletter\n\nBrand style:\nModern, clean, professional, technology-focused.\n\nThe final output must be a complete HTML document starting with <!DOCTYPE html> and ending with </html>."
        }
      },
